# ============================================================================
#  English.SystematicMIDISLanguageFile  (.SMLF)
#  Systematics TRILLION MIDI maker - English (default) language file
#  Version: 1.6.0.0
#
#  This file can be opened in any plain-text editor (Notepad, Notepad++,
#  VS Code, ...).
#
#  FORMAT
#  ------
#    - Lines beginning with '#' are comments and are ignored.
#    - Blank lines are ignored.
#    - Sections are marked with [Section Name].
#    - Every string is a line in the form:   key = value
#    - The key on the LEFT must never be changed.
#    - The value on the RIGHT is the text shown to the user - translate that.
#    - {placeholders} like {version} or {count} are replaced by the app at
#      runtime. Keep them exactly as they are (you may move them around).
#    - A line with \n inside the value is a line break (like pressing Enter
#      twice in a row is not; a single \n is a new line).
#
#  HOW TO TRANSLATE
#  ----------------
#    1. Copy this file to e.g. "Spanish.SMLF" in this same folder.
#    2. Open the copy in Notepad and translate every value (right side).
#    3. Do not translate section names, keys, or {placeholders}.
#    4. Save the file as UTF-8 (Notepad: File > Save As > Encoding: UTF-8).
#    5. The app picks the language from this folder - see the app's settings.
# ============================================================================

